sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Player
    participant UI as GameUI
    participant Game as GameController
    participant State as GameState
    participant Story as StoryController
    participant Activity as ActivityController
    participant Exam as AssessmentController
    participant Runner as JavaAssessmentRunner
    participant Save as SaveManager

    Note over Player,Save: Design proposal, not implemented gameplay. Rules and TBD IDs: Sprint1.md / Design Documents.
    opt New-game opening
        Game->>Story: playOpening(state)
        Story->>UI: Teach previous-semester Final battle against Mr. Reward
        Player->>UI: Follow tutorial interactions
        Story->>State: Record scripted defeat and opening completion
        Game->>State: Enter current semester at Day 1
    end
    Note over Game,State: Opening and Days 1-2: all penalties are warnings only, never deferred. Tutorial details T11.
    Note over Game,State: Very low SAN unlocks a bad ending. Trigger points and priority with Midterm remain T10.
    Game->>Game: beginDay()
    Game->>State: Read day plan, makeup replacement and dated effects
    State-->>Game: Course, phase, due results and early-sleep entitlement
    Game->>State: Activate this day's late-night SAN and XP-gain reductions if present
    Note over Game,State: Next-day duration is fixed, amounts and SAN interactions remain T03.
    opt Ordinary results are due after three days
        Game->>State: grades.returnDueGrades(day)
        Game->>State: replaceEstimateEffects(assessmentId)
        Note over Game,State: Estimates stay distinct from official marks. Replacement and average/SAN formulas: T02, T03, T08.
        Game->>UI: Show official marks and their one-time feedback
    end
    Game->>Story: playDueStories(state)
    Note over Story,State: Exact content, choice effects and release conditions: T14.
    opt Early-sleep bonus was earned
        Game->>State: Offer next-morning half-unit and SAN bonus
        Game->>UI: Show eligible half-time activities
        Player->>UI: Choose bonus-time activity
        UI->>Activity: hubChoice(state, activityId)
        Activity->>State: Validate and spend half-unit, scale numerical activity effects by 0.5
        Note over State,Activity: Rounding, discrete effects and eligibility details: T04.
    end
    Game->>UI: showDay(state), including today's ICS4U course
    Player->>UI: Choose attendance where a choice is permitted
    UI->>Game: chooseAttendance(attend, excused)
    alt Attempt to skip Midterm or Final
        Game->>UI: Reject skip, major assessment remains due
        Note over Game,State: A rejected skip does not create an absence or completed-course record.
    else Permitted ordinary absence
        Game->>State: Record excused status and attendance under tutorial policy
        Note over Game,State: Excused leave exempt. First two unexcused absences free, then minus 1 overall percentage point each. T02, T11.
        opt Missed ordinary assessment
            Game->>State: Record makeup requirement and next two Lesson candidates
            Note over Game,State: Replace a Lesson with the same questions, not an extra slot. Selection, collisions and late-term gaps: T05.
        end
        Game->>UI: Show attendance consequence and applicable absence route
        Note over Game,UI: Detailed use of the skipped class slot remains T04.
    else Attend the scheduled course
        alt Lesson, including a tutorial Lesson
            Game->>UI: showLesson(todayPlan)
            Game->>UI: showChoice(one configured post-content interaction)
            Note over Player,Activity: Exactly one node. This Lesson offers asking OR raising a hand, not both.
            Player->>UI: Submit the classroom choice
            UI->>Activity: lessonChoice(state, choice)
            Activity->>State: Record choice and apply configured learning/participation effects once
        else Review
            Game->>UI: Present scheduled review content
            Note over Player,Activity: Review interactions remain T14, do not invent additional Lesson nodes.
        else Original or makeup assessment
            Game->>Exam: start(state, todayPlan)
            Exam->>State: Read Coding Vibe, unit Knowledge, SAN, HP and assessment conditions
            Note over State,Exam: HP is distinct from the mark, its mapping and SAN influence are T01, T03.
            Exam->>Exam: Load fixed ordinary questions or sample Midterm/Final questions
            opt Makeup assessment
                Exam->>State: No normal Lesson bonus, apply makeup SAN debuff
                Exam->>Exam: Use original questions, disable peeking, increase cheating detection risk
            end
            Exam->>UI: showAssessment(session)
            loop Permitted interactions while assessment is active
                alt Normal assessment input
                    alt Lab
                        Player->>UI: Enter complete Java source
                        UI->>Exam: respond(state, source)
                        Exam->>Runner: compileAndTest(source, assessmentId)
                        Runner-->>Exam: Compilation and built-in-test evidence
                        Exam->>Runner: checkStyle(source, rubricId)
                        Runner-->>Exam: Coding-style evidence
                        Note over Exam,Runner: Planned evaluation only. Execution limits, errors, retries and scoring: T06.
                    else Final question-battle turn
                        Player->>UI: Submit question answer or permitted battle choice
                        UI->>Exam: respond(state, input)
                        Exam->>State: Apply defined battle effects through tutorial-aware boundary
                        Exam->>UI: Show turn feedback with HP separate from marks
                        Note over State,Exam: Turn rules, HP changes, defeat and mark mapping remain T01.
                    else Unit Test or Midterm
                        Player->>UI: Submit assessment responses
                        UI->>Exam: respond(state, input)
                        Note over Player,Exam: Fixed Unit Test versus random Midterm questions. Combat format and timing: T01, T07.
                    end
                else Reward or cheating interaction
                    opt Player uses an available reward
                        Player->>UI: Select reward
                        UI->>Exam: useReward(state, rewardId)
                    end
                    Note over Player,Exam: Item effects, consumption, use timing and detection details: T09.
                    opt Cheating is detected
                        Exam->>Exam: resolveCheating(state, serious)
                        alt Penalty-free tutorial
                            Exam->>UI: Warn only, apply no SAN loss or zero mark
                        else Normal semester
                            Exam->>State: Apply large SAN loss
                            opt Serious cheating
                                Exam->>State: grades.applySeriousCheatingZero(assessmentId)
                            end
                        end
                    end
                else Player self-estimates where applicable
                    Player->>UI: Request self-estimate during assessment
                    UI->>Exam: selfEstimate(state)
                    Exam->>State: Apply SAN cost unless tutorial, record uncertain mark and provisional effects
                    Exam->>UI: Show clearly labelled estimate, not official result
                    Note over State,Exam: Accuracy, repeat requests, immediate-exam availability and later reset: T08.
                end
            end
            Note over UI,Exam: Available actions, attempts and completion conditions remain T01, T06-T09, not unlimited retries.
            UI->>Exam: submit(state)
            Exam->>State: grades.recordSubmission(record), preserving any serious-cheating zero
            Exam-->>Game: Submission accepted with assessment record
            alt Midterm or Final
                Game->>State: grades.releaseOfficialGrade(assessmentId) immediately
                Game->>State: Replace provisional effects and apply official grade feedback once
                Game->>UI: showResult(officialRecord)
            else Ordinary Lab or Unit Test
                Exam->>State: Record official return three days after submission
                Exam->>UI: Confirm submission and pending mark
                Note over Game,State: Pending marking does not block leaving the completed class. Ordinary makeups also return marks after three days.
            end
            alt Midterm checkpoint
                Game->>State: Evaluate official grades, SAN and Retake opportunities
                Game->>UI: Show permitted Continue, Drop or Retake choices
                Note over Game,UI: Low grade plus low SAN forbids Continue. Thresholds and bad-ending priority: T10.
                Player->>UI: Choose permitted outcome
                UI->>Game: resolveMidterm(choice)
                alt Retake with an opportunity remaining
                    Game->>State: Consume one of two opportunities, keep XP, return to Day 1 with initial SAN debuff
                    Note over Game,State: Other reset data, tutorial replay and save boundary: T10-T12. Do not continue today's afternoon.
                else Drop
                    Game->>State: Record the run's ending
                else Continue is permitted
                    Game->>State: Keep current-day continuation
                end
            else Final completion
                Game->>State: Determine percentage and ending using grades, XP and SAN
                Game->>UI: showEnding(outcome)
                Note over Game,State: Formula and ending branches: T01-T03, T10. No invented playable Day 41.
            end
        end
    end
    opt ICS4U slot is resolved AND this same day continues
        Game->>State: Advance to OTHER_CLASSES
        Game->>UI: Offer focus on other class or revise ICS
        Player->>UI: Choose other-class activity
        UI->>Activity: otherClassChoice(state, choice)
        Activity->>State: Spend one slot, focus means no stat change, ICS revision means +XP and -SAN
        Note over State,Activity: Tutorial penalties warn only. XP uses today's multiplier, no other-subject Knowledge stat.
        Game->>State: Advance to AFTER_SCHOOL
        Game->>UI: Offer Hub activity or immediate sleep
        alt Sleep immediately after school
            Player->>UI: Choose sleep
            UI->>Game: chooseSleep()
            Game->>State: Record next-morning half-unit and SAN bonus, finish today's activity periods
        else Continue Hub activities
            loop AFTER_SCHOOL, EVENING, then LATE_NIGHT while awake
                Player->>UI: Choose an available activity
                UI->>Activity: hubChoice(state, activityId)
                alt Valid activity
                    Activity->>State: Spend one unit and apply configured effects once
                    Note over State,Activity: Learning, rest, entertainment and shallow relationships, exact values T04, T13.
                    opt LATE_NIGHT was used
                        Activity->>State: Record lower SAN and XP gain multiplier for next day, unless tutorial
                    end
                else Invalid activity
                    Activity->>UI: Explain rejection without spending time or changing stats
                    Note over Game,Activity: Remain in the same slot after rejection, advance only when its activity is resolved.
                end
            end
            Note over Game,UI: Other sleep/unused-slot details remain T04, no extra recovery amount is assumed.
        end
    end
    opt The run reaches a defined day-end boundary
        Game->>Game: endDay()
        Game->>UI: Show day summary without repeating effects
        Game->>Save: saveAtDayEnd(state)
        Save-->>Game: Success or failure
        Game->>UI: Show actual save status
        Note over Game,Save: Include pending marks, estimates, future effects, schedule replacements, relationships and Retake count.
        Note over Game,Save: Snapshot/advance order, failure and Drop/Retake/Final persistence boundaries remain T12. No extra save point.
    end
    opt A new playthrough is chosen after an ending
        Game->>State: Carry selected rewards only, do not inherit XP or other progress
        Note over Game,State: This is not the Midterm Retake rule. Reward selection and opening details: T09-T10.
    end
